        <exercise>
            <title>
                Two candles.
            </title>
            <p>
                A thick candle 20 cm tall and a thin candle 30 cm tall are lit at the same time. After one hour, the thick candle is 18 cm tall and the thin candle is 24 cm tall.
            </p>
            <ol>
                <li>
                    Which candle is burning faster? Faster in what sense?
                </li>
                <li>
                    Will the thin candle ever be shorter than the thick one? When?
                </li>
                <li>
                    What would you measure, and in what units, to settle these questions?
                </li>
            </ol>
            <!-- Seeds: quantity vs. number, units, rate as ratio (cm per hour) vs. amount (cm lost), constant-rate extrapolation. The "faster" ambiguity — total wax burned vs. height lost per hour — is the ratio/amount distinction stated by a situation. -->
        </exercise>

        <exercise>
            <title>
                Road trip.
            </title>
            <p>
                The odometer of a car reads the following mileage at the following times:
                <table>
                    <tabular halign="center">
                        <hrow header="yes">
                            <cell>
                                Time
                            </cell>
                            <cell>
                                Mileage
                            </cell>
                        </hrow>
                        <hrow>
                            <cell>
                                9:00am
                            </cell>
                            <cell>
                                12,480 mi
                            </cell>
                        </hrow>
                        <hrow>
                            <cell>
                                10:30am
                            </cell>
                            <cell>
                                12,551 mi
                            </cell>
                        </hrow>
                        <hrow>
                            <cell>
                                11:00am
                            </cell>
                            <cell>
                                12,590 mi
                            </cell>
                        </hrow>
                        <hrow>
                            <cell>
                                1:30pm
                            </cell>
                            <cell>
                                12,590 mi
                            </cell>
                        </hrow>
                    </tabular>
                </table>
                <ol>
                    <li>
                        What happened between 11:00 and 1:30?
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        Were they driving faster before or after 10:15? How do you know from the table?
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        Estimate the odometer at 10:00. What are you assuming?
                    </li>
                </ol>
            </p>
                <!-- Seeds: coordinating two quantities from a table, computing a rate from two readings, interpolation and its assumptions (what a table does and does not determine — forward thread to Ch. 2). -->
        </exercise>
        
